#D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]successor_offers.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/successor_offers.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-7c[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-7c/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Successor Offers contract, vectors, and docs[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: rewrite task-dependencies §12 as Successor Offers (offer [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ladder, project offers, pull-in offers, breaker deletion, selection, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pick writes, keys, JSON, CLI flags, nav picker API), add the SO vector [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]table, retire SL17/PP15/PDC2, and update capture/plan/freshness docs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plus the README, getting-started, and hooks mentions.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust planner emits offers and applies a selection[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]rust_offers[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rust_offers: change plan_successors, project_close, and project_pull_in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so every would-be link becomes a keyed offer, project residents are [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]offered, the breaker is deleted, unplanned predecessors use the implicit[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]destination, and a selection input drives link, mint, Next, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]freshness writes; port the SO vectors as unit tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob capture --pull-in, offer JSON, and the Mac guard[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]rust_capture[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rust_offers[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rust_capture: add -p/--pull-in and the hidden --require-pull-in-choice [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to bob capture, thread the selection through every close path and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]batch net pass, emit offer/pull_in JSON and numbered human rows, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cover the sase_foo case and the SO vectors with integration tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]task-status-cycler plans offers, awaits the picker, then [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]applies[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cycler_offers[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler_offers: port the offer rule to the cycler, delete [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SUCCESSOR_BREAKER_LIMIT, await nav's picker between plan and apply, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-plan with the selection against fresh text, stamp picks, guard the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]editor insertion branch, extend the reopen receipt, and fall back to a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]no-link notice without nav.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Navigation hotkeys successor picker modal and walk integration[bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]nav_picker[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav_picker: add the api.successors v1 multi-select picker (groups, muted[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows, filter, Tab/Ctrl+A marks, double-press guard, plan meter), hold [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the review-walk gesture through the picker so the walk advances once [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]after it settles, and update the unblocked notice copy.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Per-row destination override in the Obsidian picker[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]obsidian_destination[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cycler_offers, nav_picker[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]obsidian_destination: expose block-id-prompt's Pomodoro link picker as a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]versioned api, chain it from the successor picker's Ctrl+Shift+Enter to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retarget rows, and make the cycler insert picks at an overridden [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing or new entry.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture in-panel pull-in choice step[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]mac_choice[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rust_capture[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac_choice: decode offer/pull_in fields, number offer rows on the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preview cards, add a keyboard multi-select choice step on Return, pass [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]--pull-in on submit, use the --require-pull-in-choice race guard, fix [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]missing copy, and verify on macOS CI.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Decision record, supersession marks, and epic acceptance[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]decision_record[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rust_capture, cycler_offers, nav_picker, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]obsidian_destination, mac_choice[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]decision_record: record the accepted Successor Offers decision, mark the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]records it partly supersedes, optionally add the glossary term, re-run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the cross-repo acceptance checks, and record the deferred follow-ups.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-7c","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-7c.1","reasoning_effort":"high","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_nam